    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward a productive afternoon led by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jacob Wilson**, our two highest-projected starters today. **Gunnar Henderson** (74.86) remains an elite start, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Freddy Peralta and a critical +2% boost due to Peralta\u2019s slow delivery, which creates prime conditions for **Gunnar Henderson** to exploit his elite speed. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) draws the best matchup of the day against Bradford (xERA 5.29), benefiting from a significant +19% SP skill advantage and a favorable hitter's park. **Jackson Merrill** (69.72) also rounds out our top-tier targets, as his dynamic platoon edge against Bibee compensates for the middle-of-the-order slotting.\n\nWhile we are optimized for efficiency, the bench decision for **Coby Mayo** (42.34) was the most difficult pivot. **Coby Mayo** technically cleared the 40-point threshold, but he ultimately ceded his spot due to an unfavorable platoon split against Peralta and a lower order placement that suppressed his run-scoring ceiling compared to the likes of **Miguel Vargas** and **Dominic Smith**. We are also keeping a close watch on the matchup against Dylan Cease, who presents a significant challenge for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Andy Pages**. Despite the SP skill penalty from Cease, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** maintains a respectable 54.17 score due to a substantial +14% platoon adjustment. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's rotation. The matchup for **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** against Henderson is particularly daunting given the opposing pitcher's elite 2.84 xERA. While **Kyle Tucker** maintains value through his base projection, he is operating at a deficit today due to the SP skill delta. We are proceeding with the current lineup to maximize our pursuit of stolen bases and batting average, though we will be monitoring the game flow closely to manage our remaining game caps for the season. We continue to hold **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** in reserve as we navigate the final stretch.",
